From c380e64426d832d135846fe8b4cd24d9f299b125 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ARGILETTE <babalekpam@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 15:52:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Suppression gate in front of both send paths
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Node CRM has two ways to send email — the authenticated tracked-send route
and the workflow engine's send_email action, the latter unattended with
execution_mode defaulting to auto. Neither checked anything before
transmitting, no suppression list existed, tracked sends carried an open
pixel and IP logging with no opt-out link, and contacts.opt_in was read by
nothing.

Adds email_suppressions keyed (tenant_id, channel, address) as a primary
key so a repeat opt-out is a no-op, one assertSendable() called by both
paths, and RFC 8058 one-click unsubscribe with HMAC tokens that need no
storage and cannot be forged across tenants. The footer is injected inside
embedTracking rather than at the call sites, so a future third send path
inherits it.

Also fixes the tracked-email feature, which threw at runtime: db.execute()
on the node-postgres driver resolves to a pg Result, not an array, so every
'const [x] = await db.execute(...)' in those two files raised
'TypeError: is not iterable'. Adds a driver-agnostic rows() helper.

Lawful basis is now required to import a scraped prospect, enforced by a
CHECK constraint rather than app-level validation, and importing a record
no longer marks it 'contacted' when nothing was sent.
